# Release milestone: the runner's run over the public testbed's `core`, with every component at its released tag.
# Copied to tests/integration/.env.local before the run. The runner clones the components and the testbed itself and
# configures `core` as the CI testbed stage does (tests/testbed/run-testbed-stage.sh). Relative paths resolve against
# the living-doc checkout (see docs/_integration/README.md § Run a milestone target).
TARGET=testbed
# The testbed's `master`, as a full commit SHA: git ls-remote https://github.com/AbsaOSS/living-doc-testbed master
TESTBED_REF=36a0ee65ad11df7588cd74a505ea1ace1ef7abc9
# Each component at the tag `living-doc` v0.1.0 lists, the same tags tests/collector/collector-pins.env pins.
COLLECTOR_GH_REF=v0.2.0
TOOLKIT_REF=v0.1.0
GENERATOR_MARKDOWN_REF=v0.1.0
OUT_DIR=docs/_integration/MS3/testbed-core
# Empty tries python3, then python. On Git Bash for Windows, python3 may be the Microsoft Store alias: set
# PYTHON=python.
PYTHON=python
